In the second code snippet, this output statement generates an assertion that checks if the return value `New_Ret` (`ArrList.Contains(x)`) is `true` and if either the index of `x` in the newly constructed array is greater than or equal to 0 (`New_arrListIndexOfX`) or the last index of `x` is greater than or equal to 0 (`New_arrListLastIndexOfX`). So, it checks if `x` is contained in the array and its first or last occurrence position in the array respectively.--------------------
